## Additional Use Grant

Subject to all terms and conditions of this License, Particular LLC grants you permission to make Production Use of the Licensed Work solely for Permitted Application Use, as defined below.

No Production Use is granted except as expressly stated in this Additional Use Grant or in a separate written commercial license from Particular LLC.

## 1. Permitted Application Use

“Permitted Application Use” means using the Licensed Work, or a modified version or derivative work that is not a Compliance-Reduced Build, Circumvention Build, Hosted Mohio Service, Standalone Mohio Offering, Competing Mohio Offering, or Commercial Mohio Platform, to:

(a) develop, compile, interpret, test, operate, and maintain Applications;

(b) make internal Production Use of Applications within your organization and entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control with your organization;

(c) host and operate Applications for customers or other third parties, provided the hosted offering is the Application itself and does not provide general-purpose access to MOHIO compilation, interpretation, runtime execution, deployment, hosting, serving, management, development-tooling, profile marketplace, langmap marketplace, compliance services, audit services, certification services, or app-serving-platform capabilities;

(d) license, sell, or otherwise distribute Applications to customers or end users, provided that the Application is not a Hosted Mohio Service, Standalone Mohio Offering, Competing Mohio Offering, Commercial Mohio Platform, Compliance-Reduced Build, or Circumvention Build;

(e) reproduce and distribute Runtime Components in object-code form solely as incorporated into, and reasonably necessary to operate, an Application, provided that you comply with the notice and license-display requirements of this License and the runtime distribution scope in `LICENSE-SCOPE.md` for the applicable release; and

(f) connect an Application to official MOHIO services, paid services, langmap services, sector profile services, compliance services, audit services, entitlement services, APIs, marketplaces, certification services, or managed services only as permitted by the applicable service terms, subscription terms, commercial agreement, enterprise agreement, or written authorization from Particular LLC.

You may modify the Licensed Work and make Production Use of the modified version under this Additional Use Grant only if the modified version remains within Permitted Application Use and is not used for any Excluded Production Use.

For clarity, this License is intended to allow you to build, run, host, and sell your own Applications using the Mohio Public Core. It is not intended to allow you to offer Mohio itself, or a substantially similar compiler, runtime, hosted service, server, app-serving platform, studio, IDE, profile marketplace, langmap marketplace, certification service, compliance service, audit service, managed runtime, or competing language platform, without a separate written commercial license from Particular LLC.

## 2. Excluded Production Uses

No Production Use is granted under this Additional Use Grant for any of the following uses. A separate written commercial license from Particular LLC is required for any such Production Use:

(i) a Hosted Mohio Service;

(ii) a Standalone Mohio Offering;

(iii) a Competing Mohio Offering;

(iv) a Commercial Mohio Platform;

(v) a Compliance-Reduced Build;

(vi) a Circumvention Build;

(vii) a paid, subscription, supported, hosted, managed, service-bureau, timesharing, marketplace, consulting-delivery, or commercial service that allows third parties to submit, compile, interpret, execute, deploy, host, serve, manage, test, debug, optimize, profile, transform, translate, audit, certify, validate, or operate arbitrary Mohio source code or Mohio programs;

(viii) a hosted compiler, hosted interpreter, hosted runtime, app server, managed execution service, development environment, IDE, studio, app-serving platform, profile marketplace, langmap marketplace, connector marketplace, audit service, compliance service, certification service, training platform, or managed platform whose primary or material functionality is based on the Licensed Work or provides MOHIO as a platform;

(ix) redistribution, sublicensing, resale, rental, leasing, managed-service use, timesharing, service-bureau use, consulting-delivery use, or commercial operation of the Licensed Work as a product, platform, runtime, compiler, interpreter, server, developer tool, studio, app-serving system, hosted service, or managed service rather than as an incidental runtime component of an Application permitted by Section 1;

(x) removal, bypass, disabling, weakening, alteration, substitution, or circumvention of service gates, entitlement checks, subscription checks, paid-feature checks, certification checks, signature checks, audit controls, compliance controls, langmap access controls, profile access controls, sector-profile controls, usage limits, official service calls, or other protected functionality;

(xi) use of the Licensed Work to create, train, benchmark, validate, operate, support, or improve a product or service intended to replace, replicate, compete with, or provide a substitute for a MOHIO product or service offered, commercially released, publicly announced, or expressly identified by Particular LLC in `RESERVED-COMMERCIAL-OFFERINGS.md` as a reserved commercial offering, including MOHIO Enterprise, MOHIO Studio, MOHIO Flow, MOHIO Cloud, MOHIO Hosting, MOHIO Server, Get Mohio, official langmap services, official sector profile services, official compliance services, official audit services, certification services, managed runtime services, or commercial platform services;

(xii) use of the Licensed Work to provide custom compiler files, modified runtime files, modified interpreter files, stripped compliance controls, disabled audit controls, altered sector-profile behavior, modified profile loaders, unofficial certification tooling, hosted app-serving systems, or managed Mohio execution services to customers or third parties as a product or service;

(xiii) any use that violates applicable service terms, subscription terms, enterprise terms, profile terms, langmap terms, API terms, certification terms, trademark terms, or written agreements with Particular LLC.

Contact legal@particularllc.com for commercial licensing.

## 3. Definitions

### 3.1 Production Use

“Production Use” means use of the Licensed Work for internal business operations, revenue-generating activity, customer-facing operations, delivery of products or services to third parties, hosted services, managed services, commercial distribution, or any use other than development, testing, evaluation, demonstration, education, research, or other non-production use already permitted by this License.

### 3.2 Application

“Application” means a software program, product, or service developed by or for you that uses the Licensed Work but whose primary purpose is to provide functionality other than general-purpose compilation, interpretation, execution, deployment, hosting, serving, management, development, transformation, translation, certification, auditing, compliance verification, app-serving, or operation of Mohio source code or Mohio programs for third parties.

An Application may be commercial, customer-facing, hosted, or distributed, provided that it does not become a Hosted Mohio Service, Standalone Mohio Offering, Competing Mohio Offering, Commercial Mohio Platform, Compliance-Reduced Build, or Circumvention Build.

### 3.3 Runtime Components

“Runtime Components” means the portions of the Licensed Work expressly identified as redistributable runtime components in `LICENSE-SCOPE.md` included with the applicable release.

### 3.4 Hosted Mohio Service

“Hosted Mohio Service” means a hosted service, managed service, platform, API, app server, cloud service, development environment, IDE, studio, marketplace, training environment, or other service through which a third party can submit, compile, interpret, execute, deploy, host, serve, test, debug, manage, translate, transform, optimize, profile, certify, audit, validate, or otherwise operate arbitrary Mohio source code or Mohio programs, or otherwise obtain general-purpose access to the material compiler, interpreter, runtime, deployment, hosting, serving, app-serving, development-tool, profile, langmap, compliance, audit, certification, or management capabilities of the Licensed Work.

A service is not a Hosted Mohio Service merely because an Application built with the Licensed Work is hosted, is customer-facing, or exposes an application-specific API. A feature limited to configuring or extending the specific business functionality of an Application is not a Hosted Mohio Service unless it provides general-purpose access to Mohio compilation, interpretation, execution, deployment, hosting, serving, runtime management, profile management, langmap management, audit services, compliance services, certification services, or app-serving-platform functionality.

### 3.5 Standalone Mohio Offering

“Standalone Mohio Offering” means a product or service offered to third parties in which the Licensed Work, or a derivative work of it, is separately accessible or is a principal component providing general-purpose Mohio compilation, interpretation, execution, runtime, deployment, hosting, serving, app-serving, development-tool, profile, langmap, compliance, audit, certification, translation, transformation, or management functionality, rather than an incidental component of an Application.

### 3.6 Competing Mohio Offering

“Competing Mohio Offering” means any product or service that is marketed, provided, sold, distributed, hosted, supported, or made available as a practical substitute for a MOHIO product or service offered, commercially released, publicly announced, or expressly identified by Particular LLC in `RESERVED-COMMERCIAL-OFFERINGS.md` as a reserved commercial offering, including MOHIO Enterprise, MOHIO Studio, MOHIO Flow, MOHIO Cloud, MOHIO Hosting, MOHIO Server, Get Mohio, official langmap services, official sector profile services, official compliance services, official audit services, certification services, managed runtime services, or commercial platform services.

A product or service may be a Competing Mohio Offering even if it is offered without charge, offered through a different interface, offered on a different technical platform, offered as a consulting deliverable, offered as a managed service, offered as part of a larger platform, or described using different terminology.

For clarity, a product or service is not a Competing Mohio Offering merely because it is an Application built with the Licensed Work and provides application-specific functionality to end users, provided that the product or service remains within Permitted Application Use and does not provide MOHIO itself as a hosted compiler, runtime, interpreter, server, studio, development environment, managed platform, profile marketplace, langmap marketplace, compliance service, audit service, certification service, or substantially similar language platform.

### 3.7 Commercial Mohio Platform

“Commercial Mohio Platform” means any paid, subscription, hosted, managed, customer-facing, marketplace, service-bureau, timesharing, resale, sublicensing, consulting-delivery, supported, or commercial offering that provides MOHIO compilation, interpretation, execution, deployment, hosting, serving, app-server, app-serving, development-tooling, studio, IDE, langmap, sector profile, compliance, audit, certification, connector, managed runtime, or platform capabilities to third parties as a material feature of the offering.

### 3.8 Official Release

“Official Release” means the unmodified release of the Licensed Work first publicly distributed by Particular LLC and identified by its release version, release manifest, authenticated source-control tag, and applicable `LICENSE-SCOPE.md`.

### 3.9 Official Control Materials

“Official Control Materials” means the control manifests, control tests, release manifests, signature files, certification materials, profile manifests, langmap manifests, policy files, entitlement descriptors, and other materials identified by Particular LLC as official control materials for the applicable Official Release.

### 3.10 Designated Control

“Designated Control” means a compiler, interpreter, runtime, audit, compliance, certification, entitlement, profile, sector-profile, langmap, signature, diagnostic, or service-enforcement mechanism identified as a Designated Control in the Official Control Materials for the applicable Official Release.

### 3.11 Normative Control Test

“Normative Control Test” means a test, expected result, test identifier, validation rule, certification rule, compliance rule, audit rule, diagnostic rule, profile rule, sector-profile rule, langmap rule, or runtime rule designated as normative in the Official Control Materials for the applicable Official Release.

### 3.12 Compliance-Reduced Build

“Compliance-Reduced Build” means a modified version or derivative work of the Licensed Work that, under materially equivalent supported inputs, configuration, dependencies, profiles, langmaps, official control materials, and operating conditions, does one or more of the following:

1. causes a Designated Control to fail an applicable Normative Control Test;
2. permits compilation, interpretation, execution, storage, transmission, deletion, disclosure, completion, certification, validation, approval, or app-serving of an operation that the Official Release would reject, block, fail, warn against, flag, restrict, audit, log, or require to be handled solely because of an applicable Designated Control;
3. removes, disables, bypasses, weakens, masks, substitutes, or changes from mandatory to optional a Designated Control that is mandatory in the Official Release under the same applicable profile, sector profile, langmap, documented configuration, or official control material;
4. suppresses, falsifies, materially alters, materially delays, omits, or misrepresents a required audit event, compliance result, diagnostic, failure, warning, policy result, profile result, sector-profile result, langmap result, certification result, control-status output, entitlement result, or signature result produced by a Designated Control;
5. introduces an undocumented mechanism, configuration, code path, hook, dependency substitution, runtime condition, profile substitution, sector-profile substitution, langmap substitution, entitlement bypass, signing-key substitution, external service substitution, or alternate control material that produces any result described in paragraphs 1 through 4; or
6. represents, markets, supports, distributes, hosts, or operates the modified version as preserving official compliance, certification, audit, compatibility, langmap, profile, sector-profile, or runtime status when it does not pass all applicable Normative Control Tests.

A build is not a Compliance-Reduced Build solely because its source-code or object-code hashes differ from the Official Release.

A modification that affects only unrelated functionality, strengthens a Designated Control, corrects a defect, improves diagnostics, improves security, or improves reliability is not a Compliance-Reduced Build if the modified build continues to pass all applicable Normative Control Tests and remains at least as restrictive as the Official Release with respect to the applicable Designated Controls.

Use of a configuration option expressly permitted by the Official Control Materials and official documentation for the applicable release does not, by itself, create a Compliance-Reduced Build.

Modification, replacement, or removal of a local copy of the Official Control Materials does not alter which controls and tests apply to the applicable Official Release.

### 3.13 Circumvention Build

“Circumvention Build” means a modified version or derivative work of the Licensed Work, or any associated code, patch, plugin, script, service, configuration, documentation, instruction, or mechanism, designed or used to bypass, disable, avoid, remove, replace, weaken, defeat, or circumvent service gates, entitlement checks, subscription checks, paid-feature checks, certification checks, signature checks, audit controls, compliance controls, langmap access controls, sector profile access controls, usage limits, official service calls, or protected functionality.

A separate written commercial license from Particular LLC is required for Production Use of any Licensed Work in connection with a Circumvention Build.

## 4. Application Code, User Code, and Output

Particular LLC claims no copyright ownership in source code, application code, data, prompts, configuration, outputs, artifacts, or other original material created by you merely because it was authored in, processed by, compiled by, interpreted by, executed using, transformed by, served by, or operated with the Licensed Work.

Any portion of the Licensed Work copied into, linked into, embedded in, packaged with, distributed with, or required to operate an Application remains subject to this License.

## 5. Commercial Services, Official Profiles, and Official Langmaps

Official MOHIO services, paid services, hosted services, enterprise services, managed services, official langmaps, official sector profiles, certified profiles, custom profiles, compliance profiles, policy packs, profile-generation systems, certification services, official connectors, and advanced compliance, audit, entitlement, cost-optimization, governance, or profile services are not included in this License unless expressly identified in `LICENSE-SCOPE.md` for the applicable release.

Access to those services or materials requires the applicable service terms, subscription terms, commercial agreement, enterprise agreement, profile terms, langmap terms, API terms, certification terms, or written authorization from Particular LLC.

